I couldn't see the body of `decideSwap` (lines 381–396), so I couldn't write a SEARCH that I knew would match. Instead I appended a wrapper at the end of `src/rota.ts`. It calls the existing `decideSwap` first, so any throw happens before anything changes. After a successful approval, it refuses the other pending requests for that shift, copying the approved request's `decidedAt`. Refusals, other shifts and already-decided requests are left alone.

It relies on the private `swaps` array and assumes the original stores and updates the request in place. Once you can open the file, folding this logic straight into `decideSwap` would be cleaner. I can write that edit if you paste the method.
